<title>SAN MARINO: San Marino legalises homosexuality.</title>
<headline>San Marino legalises homosexuality.</headline>
<dateline>SAN MARINO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Marino, the world's oldest and smallest republic, legalised homosexuality on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Parliamentarians in the tiny mountain state near Italy's northern Adriatic coast decided by 28 votes to 21 to scrap statutes which had banned &quot;libidinous acts with persons of the same sex&quot;. There was one abstention.</p>
<p>Homosexuality in San Marino, which dates its foundation as a republic to the year 301, had been punishable by prison sentences of up to a year.</p>
